# SmartGrow Strict Rules for AI Agents & Developers

You MUST strictly follow these rules when working on this repository:

1. BEFORE CREATING ANY CODE (SEARCH FIRST):
   - You MUST search and inspect the codebase to check if a component, utility, hook, or pattern already exists.
   - If an existing helper, hook, or component exists, REUSE IT. Do NOT create duplicate functions or components.
   - Read docs/CONTRIBUTING.md and docs/design-guide.md completely.
   - Place components in their designated folders:
     - src/config/ (constants, settings)
     - src/context/ (React context definitions)
     - src/hooks/ (custom hooks: useTheme, useAuth)
     - src/interface/ (data interfaces & contracts)
     - src/middleware/ (route guards, auth gates)
     - src/providers/ (context providers)
     - src/services/ (Axios API calls: user.api.ts)
     - src/types/ (types, enums, unions)
     - src/utils/ (pure helpers, axios.ts, localstorage.ts)
     - src/components/atoms/ (base atoms & atoms/application/)
     - src/components/molecules/ (molecules/skeleton/)
     - src/components/organisms/ (feature blocks: organisms/auth/)
     - src/components/templates/ (layouts)
     - src/components/pages/ (minimal route entry points)

2. COMPONENT REUSE (STRICT - NO DUPLICATES):
   - ALWAYS reuse existing components. Do NOT create custom tables, paginations, or modals.
   - Data Tables: MUST use ApplicationTable (@/components/atoms/application).
   - Pagination: MUST use ApplicationPagination (@/components/atoms/application).
   - Dialogs: MUST use ApplicationDialog (@/components/atoms/application).
   - Table Skeleton: MUST use TableSkeleton (@/components/molecules/skeleton).
   - ShadCN Primitives: Reuse existing in packages/ui or add via npx shadcn@latest add <name> -y.

3. SKELETON LOADING (MANDATORY FOR EVERY NEW DATA-FETCHING COMPONENT):
   - Every new organism or page section that fetches data MUST have a corresponding skeleton.
   - Skeleton file naming: ProductCard.tsx -> ProductCardSkeleton.tsx
   - Place skeleton in src/components/molecules/skeleton/ and export from its index.ts
   - Use <Skeleton /> from @workspace/ui/components/skeleton for shimmer effect.

4. MOBILE RESPONSIVE DESIGN (MANDATORY):
   - Every component, page, and organism MUST be fully mobile responsive.
   - Use Tailwind breakpoint prefixes mobile-first: default styles for mobile, sm:/md:/lg: for larger screens.
   - Use CSS Grid and Flexbox for layouts. Never use fixed pixel widths for full-width containers.
   - Wrap ApplicationTable in a horizontally scrollable container: <div className="w-full overflow-x-auto">.
   - Test design intent at: 375px (mobile), 768px (tablet), 1280px (desktop).

5. STYLING & THEME:
   - All colors come from packages/ui/src/styles/globals.css.
   - Primary action buttons MUST use .btn-primary (Brand Green #7EA817 Light / #7C9A3D Dark).
   - Secondary actions: .btn-secondary, Filters/Bordered: .btn-outline, Cancel/Ghost: .btn-ghost.

6. AFTER CODING (MANDATORY VERIFICATION):
   - You MUST run `npm run typecheck` and `npm run build` and ensure both exit with 0 errors before completing your task.
   - Never leave broken imports or TypeScript type errors.
